   'Viola honors U.S. Army Staff Sgt. Alex Viola, 29, of Keller, Texas, an engineer with the 3rd Battalion, 7th Special Forces Group. He was killed on Nov. 17, 2013, in Kandahar Province, Afghanistan, from wounds caused by an improvised explosive device. He trained at many CrossFit affiliates, and his favorite movements included pull-ups, power snatches and power cleans.

You get 20 minutes to complete as many rounds as you can of a 400 m run, 11 power snatches, 17 pull-ups and 13 power cleans, with one barbell at 95 lb / 65 lb. The load is light, but 24 barbell reps and 17 pull-ups every round tax your grip, and the run gives you little time to recover before the bar again.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "Hold a pace you can repeat every round. Use the run to shake out your grip."}, {"name": "Power Snatches", "reps": "11", "tip": "Wide grip, bar close, catch above parallel. Quick touch-and-go reps or fast singles.", "rx_men": "95 lb", "rx_women": "65 lb"}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "17", "tip": "Chin clears the bar. Break into small sets before your grip fails."}, {"name": "Power Cleans", "reps": "13", "tip": "Catch the bar on your shoulders above parallel. Keep your back flat on every pull.", "rx_men": "95 lb", "rx_women": "65 lb"}]'::jsonb,
