   'Wade honors U.S. Army Spc. Andrew Wade of Antioch, Illinois, a weapons specialist with the 1st Battalion, 87th Infantry Regiment, 10th Mountain Division. He died on March 9, 2011, in Bagram, Afghanistan, during Operation Enduring Freedom. He loved soccer and CrossFit, and his favorite workouts were built on bodyweight moves like pull-ups, push-ups and dips.

You wear a 20 lb vest or body armor and run 1,200 m, then do 4 rounds of 12 strict pull-ups, 9 strict dips and 6 strict handstand push-ups, then run another 1,200 m. Every rep is strict, so there is no kip to save your arms. The 48 pull-ups, 36 dips and 24 handstand push-ups in a vest are the real test.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "1,200 m", "tip": "Start steady. Your upper body does the heavy work in the middle.", "rx_men": "20 lb vest", "rx_women": "20 lb vest"}, {"name": "Strict Pull-Ups", "reps": "4 rounds of 12", "tip": "No kip. Start from a dead hang and pull until your chin clears the bar.", "rx_men": "20 lb vest", "rx_women": "20 lb vest"}, {"name": "Strict Ring Dips", "reps": "4 rounds of 9", "tip": "No kip. Lower until your shoulders are below your elbows, then press to lockout. CrossFit does not say rings or bars, so parallel bars are fine too.", "rx_men": "20 lb vest", "rx_women": "20 lb vest"}, {"name": "Strict Handstand Push-Ups", "reps": "4 rounds of 6", "tip": "No kip. Lower your head to the floor or mat and press to full lockout.", "rx_men": "20 lb vest", "rx_women": "20 lb vest"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "1,200 m", "tip": "Your arms are tired, not your legs. Push the pace if you can.", "rx_men": "20 lb vest", "rx_women": "20 lb vest"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
