   'Walsh honors U.S. Army 1st Lt. Jonathan P. Walsh, 28, of Cobb, Georgia, of the 2nd Battalion, 504th Infantry, 82nd Airborne Division, based at Fort Bragg, North Carolina. He died on April 22, 2012, in Paktia, Afghanistan, when enemy forces attacked his unit with an improvised explosive device.

You complete 4 rounds of 22 burpee pull-ups, 22 back squats (185 lb / 125 lb) and a 200 m run holding a plate overhead (45 lb / 25 lb). That is 88 burpee pull-ups and 88 heavy back squats. The squats come right after the burpees, while your legs and lungs are already working, and the overhead run punishes tired shoulders.',
   '[{"name": "Burpee Pull-Ups", "reps": "22", "tip": "Chest to the floor, jump to the bar and pull until your chin clears it. Find a steady rhythm."}, {"name": "Back Squats", "reps": "22", "tip": "Squat below parallel with your chest up. Use a rack with safety arms and break the set early.", "rx_men": "185 lb", "rx_women": "125 lb"}, {"name": "Plate Run", "reps": "200 m", "tip": "Hold the plate overhead with locked arms for the whole run. Walk if you must, but keep it up.", "rx_men": "45 lb plate overhead", "rx_women": "25 lb plate overhead"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Pace the burpee pull-ups, do not race them", "Break the 22 back squats into sets from round one", "Keep the plate locked out overhead on the run"]'::jsonb,
