You run 800 m carrying a 25 lb plate, then do 14 rounds of 5 strict pull-ups, 4 burpee box jumps (24 in) and 3 cleans (185 lb), then run another 800 m with the plate. That is 70 strict pull-ups and 42 heavy cleans. CrossFit lists men''s loads only, so women choose their own.',
   '[{"name": "Plate Run", "reps": "800 m", "tip": "Hold the plate any way you like. Run steady, because 14 rounds come next.", "rx_men": "25 lb plate"}, {"name": "Strict Pull-Ups", "reps": "5", "tip": "No kip. Start from a dead hang and pull until your chin clears the bar."}, {"name": "Burpee Box Jumps", "reps": "4", "tip": "Chest to the floor, then jump onto the box and stand tall. Step down.", "rx_men": "24 in"}, {"name": "Cleans", "reps": "3", "tip": "Power or squat clean, your choice. Quick singles with a flat back.", "rx_men": "185 lb"}, {"name": "Plate Run", "reps": "800 m", "tip": "Last effort. Hold the plate close to your chest if your grip is tired.", "rx_men": "25 lb plate"}]'::jsonb,
