   'CrossFit gives only the men''s Rx of a 25 lb plate, 24 in box and 185 lb cleans. Women often use a 20 in box and 125 lb cleans; note what you used. Scale the cleans to 135 lb / 95 lb or less, use banded or jumping pull-ups, and cut to 8 to 10 rounds.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Wes workout?", "answer": "For time: run 800 m with a plate, then 14 rounds of 5 strict pull-ups, 4 burpee box jumps and 3 cleans, then run 800 m with a plate. The men''s Rx is a 25 lb plate, a 24 in box and 185 lb cleans."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Wes?", "answer": "168 reps: 70 strict pull-ups, 56 burpee box jumps and 42 cleans, plus 1,600 m of running with a plate."}, {"question": "What are the women''s loads for Wes?", "answer": "CrossFit lists men''s loads only. Many athletes use a 20 in box and 125 lb cleans; note your loads with your time."}, {"question": "Who was Wes?", "answer": "U.S. Navy Lt. J. Wesley \"Wes\" Van Dorn, 29, of Greensboro, North Carolina. He died on Jan. 8, 2014, of injuries sustained in a helicopter crash off the coast of Virginia."}]'::jsonb,
