You start a 35-minute clock and run 800 m. With the time left, you complete as many rounds as you can of 8 box jumps, 6 strict pull-ups and a 21 yd walking lunge with a 45 lb plate overhead. The overhead lunge is the slow part, and your shoulders tire long before your legs. CrossFit does not give a box height or a women''s plate weight, so note what you use.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "800 m", "tip": "Run at a strong but steady pace. Every second saved goes into the AMRAP."}, {"name": "Box Jumps", "reps": "8", "tip": "Land softly with your whole foot on the box and stand tall. CrossFit does not give a box height."}, {"name": "Strict Pull-Ups", "reps": "6", "tip": "No kip. Start from a dead hang and pull until your chin clears the bar."}, {"name": "Overhead Walking Lunges", "reps": "21 yd", "tip": "Lock the plate overhead, back knee kisses the floor, and keep your ribs down.", "rx_men": "45 lb plate"}]'::jsonb,
