You complete 5 rounds of a 1,000 m row, a 200 m farmers carry, a 50 m dumbbell waiters walk with your right arm and a 50 m waiters walk with your left arm. The dumbbells are 45 lb / 30 lb. That is 5,000 m of rowing and 1,500 m of carrying. Grip, posture and shoulder stability decide your time more than speed does.',
   '[{"name": "Row", "reps": "1,000 m", "tip": "Drive with your legs first. Hold a pace you can repeat for all 5 rounds."}, {"name": "Dumbbell Farmers Carry", "reps": "200 m", "tip": "Dumbbells at your sides, shoulders back, short quick steps.", "rx_men": "45 lb dumbbells", "rx_women": "30 lb dumbbells"}, {"name": "Waiter''s Walk", "reps": "50 m right arm", "tip": "Waiters walk: one dumbbell locked out overhead in your right hand. Keep your ribs down and walk tall.", "rx_men": "45 lb", "rx_women": "30 lb"}, {"name": "Waiter''s Walk", "reps": "50 m left arm", "tip": "Switch to your left arm. Keep the biceps by your ear and the dumbbell stacked over your shoulder.", "rx_men": "45 lb", "rx_women": "30 lb"}]'::jsonb,
