   'Whitt honors Specialist Jeffery Ryan Whitt, 27, who served in Afghanistan with the Iowa Army National Guard as a forward observer. As CrossFit states, he died by suicide on Oct. 31, 2015, due to the effects of combat deployment, traumatic brain injuries, blast-wave injuries and post-traumatic stress disorder. He loved reading, the outdoors and cheering on the University of Kentucky Wildcats.

You complete 3 rounds of an 800 m run with a medicine ball, 30 wall-ball shots and 30 ball slams, all with one ball (30 lb / 20 lb). Carrying the ball for 2,400 m tires your arms before the wall balls, and the heavy ball turns 180 reps into a long grind. CrossFit does not give a wall-ball target height, so note the target you use.

If you or someone you know is struggling, call or text 988 (Veterans: press 1).',
   '[{"name": "Medicine Ball Run", "reps": "800 m", "tip": "Hug the ball at your chest and run steady. Switch how you hold it to rest your arms.", "rx_men": "30 lb ball", "rx_women": "20 lb ball"}, {"name": "Wall Balls", "reps": "30", "tip": "Full squat and drive the ball to the target. CrossFit does not give a target height.", "rx_men": "30 lb ball", "rx_women": "20 lb ball"}, {"name": "Medicine Ball Slams", "reps": "30", "tip": "Lift the ball overhead, slam it down with your whole body, and squat to pick it up with a flat back.", "rx_men": "30 lb ball", "rx_women": "20 lb ball"}]'::jsonb,
