You complete 3 rounds of an 800 m run, 5 front squats (225 lb / 155 lb), a 200 m run, 11 chest-to-bar pull-ups, a 400 m run and 12 kettlebell swings (70 lb / 53 lb). That is 4,200 m of running between short, heavy sets. The front squats are the heaviest part, so arrive at the bar with enough breath to brace.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "800 m", "tip": "Steady pace. You run 1,400 m every round."}, {"name": "Front Squats", "reps": "5", "tip": "Elbows up, chest tall, squat below parallel. Use a rack and take singles if needed.", "rx_men": "225 lb", "rx_women": "155 lb"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "200 m", "tip": "A short run to shake out your legs before the pull-ups."}, {"name": "Chest-to-Bar Pull-Ups", "reps": "11", "tip": "Your chest must touch the bar on every rep. Break into small sets."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "Keep moving. Settle your breathing for the swings."}, {"name": "Kettlebell Swings", "reps": "12", "tip": "Snap your hips and swing the bell overhead with straight arms.", "rx_men": "70 lb", "rx_women": "53 lb"}]'::jsonb,
