   'time',
   'Woehlke honors firefighter Brian Woehlke, 29, of Detroit, Michigan, who died at the scene of a fire in Westland, Michigan, on May 8, 2013. He graduated from the Schoolcraft Fire Program in 2008 and joined the Western Wayne Fire Authority in 2012.

You do 3 rounds, each for time, of 4 jerks, 5 front squats and 6 power cleans (185 lb / 125 lb), then 40 pull-ups, 50 push-ups and 60 sit-ups. You rest 3 minutes between rounds. The barbell work is short and heavy, then 150 bodyweight reps follow. Each round is its own sprint, so you can push harder than in a single long effort.',
   '[{"name": "Jerks", "reps": "4", "tip": "Push jerk or split jerk, your choice. Dip, drive and lock out overhead.", "rx_men": "185 lb", "rx_women": "125 lb"}, {"name": "Front Squats", "reps": "5", "tip": "Elbows up, chest tall, squat below parallel.", "rx_men": "185 lb", "rx_women": "125 lb"}, {"name": "Power Cleans", "reps": "6", "tip": "Catch above parallel with a flat back. Singles are fine at this load.", "rx_men": "185 lb", "rx_women": "125 lb"}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "40", "tip": "Chin clears the bar. Break into sets before your grip fails."}, {"name": "Push-Ups", "reps": "50", "tip": "Chest to the floor and lock out at the top. Small sets early."}, {"name": "Sit-Ups", "reps": "60", "tip": "Touch the floor behind your head and your feet at the top."}, {"name": "Rest", "reps": "3 min", "isRest": true, "tip": "Rest between rounds. Start the next round when 3 minutes are up."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record the time for each of the 3 rounds. CrossFit does not say whether to score the total or each round, so many athletes log all three times and their sum.',
