   'Lower the barbell to 135 lb / 95 lb or less. Use banded pull-ups or ring rows, and push-ups from your knees or with hands on a box. Halve the pull-ups, push-ups and sit-ups, or do 2 rounds.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Woehlke workout?", "answer": "3 rounds, each for time, of 4 jerks, 5 front squats and 6 power cleans (185 lb / 125 lb), 40 pull-ups, 50 push-ups and 60 sit-ups, with 3 minutes of rest between rounds."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Woehlke?", "answer": "495 reps: 12 jerks, 15 front squats, 18 power cleans, 120 pull-ups, 150 push-ups and 180 sit-ups."}, {"question": "How do I score Woehlke?", "answer": "Time each round. CrossFit does not say whether the score is the total or each round, so log all three times."}, {"question": "Who was Woehlke?", "answer": "Firefighter Brian Woehlke, 29, of Detroit, Michigan, of the Western Wayne Fire Authority. He died at the scene of a fire in Westland, Michigan, on May 8, 2013."}]'::jsonb,
