   'time',
   'Wyk honors Army Pfc. Jacob H. "Wyk" Wykstra, 21, of Thornton, Colorado, of the 1st Battalion, 12th Infantry Regiment, 4th Infantry Division. He died on May 28, 2014, in Kandahar Province, Afghanistan, of injuries sustained in an aircraft accident.

You complete 5 rounds of 5 front squats (225 lb / 155 lb), 5 rope climbs to 15 ft and a 400 m run carrying a plate (45 lb / 25 lb). That is 25 heavy front squats and 25 rope climbs. The rope climbs drain your grip and arms, and the plate run gives them little rest before the bar again.',
   '[{"name": "Front Squats", "reps": "5", "tip": "Elbows up, chest tall, squat below parallel. Use a rack and take singles if needed.", "rx_men": "225 lb", "rx_women": "155 lb"}, {"name": "Rope Climbs", "reps": "5", "tip": "Use your feet to clamp the rope and stand up. Climb down hand over hand."}, {"name": "Plate Run", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "Hold the plate any way you like. Hug it at your chest to save your grip.", "rx_men": "45 lb plate", "rx_women": "25 lb plate"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Rack the bar for the front squats", "Use your legs on every rope climb", "Hug the plate on the run"]'::jsonb,
   '["Set the barbell in a rack so you can walk it out each round.", "Brace hard before each front squat and keep your elbows high.", "Use a foot lock on the rope so your legs do most of the work; 25 climbs will wreck your arms otherwise.", "Rest a breath at the bottom between rope climbs rather than failing near the top.", "Hold the plate high on your chest so it does not pull your shoulders forward on the run."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the front squat to 155 lb / 105 lb or less. Replace rope climbs with lying-to-standing rope pulls or climbs to a lower height, or cut to 3 per round. Use a lighter plate.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Wyk workout?", "answer": "5 rounds for time of 5 front squats (225 lb / 155 lb), 5 rope climbs to 15 ft and a 400 m run with a plate (45 lb / 25 lb)."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Wyk?", "answer": "50 reps: 25 front squats and 25 rope climbs, plus 2,000 m of running with a plate."}, {"question": "How do I carry the plate?", "answer": "CrossFit does not say, so hold it any way you like and keep moving."}, {"question": "Who was Wyk?", "answer": "Army Pfc. Jacob H. \"Wyk\" Wykstra, 21, of Thornton, Colorado, of the 4th Infantry Division. He died on May 28, 2014, in Kandahar Province, Afghanistan."}]'::jsonb,
