   'time',
   'Zembiec honors U.S. Marine Corps Maj. Douglas A. Zembiec, 34, of Albuquerque, New Mexico, assigned to Headquarters Battalion, Marine Corps National Capital Region, Henderson Hall, in Arlington, Virginia. He was killed during a firefight on May 11, 2007, in Baghdad, Iraq.

You complete 5 rounds of 11 back squats (185 lb / 125 lb), 7 strict burpee pull-ups and a 400 m run. Each burpee pull-up includes a strict push-up, then a jump to a bar ideally 12 in above your max standing reach, then a strict pull-up. The strict rules make 35 burpee pull-ups far harder than they sound, and the squats tire your legs for the jump.',
   '[{"name": "Back Squats", "reps": "11", "tip": "Squat below parallel with your chest up. Use a rack with safety arms.", "rx_men": "185 lb", "rx_women": "125 lb"}, {"name": "Strict Burpee Pull-Ups", "reps": "7", "tip": "Strict push-up at the bottom, jump to a bar about 12 in above your standing reach, then a strict pull-up with no kip."}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "Settle your breathing and shake out your arms before the squats."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Set the bar 12 in above your standing reach", "Break the back squats into sets early", "No kip on the burpee pull-ups"]'::jsonb,
